.TH FF 1.SH NAMEff \- find files by name.SH SYNOPSIS\fBff\fRname.SH DESCRIPTION\fBff\fRfinds the files whose names contain\fIname\fRanywhere under the current directory.  It does it by building thecommand\fBdir \-ausr ! grep \fIname\fRand handing that to a module called\fBshell\fR,\fRthe one your own OS-9 brings; without one resident it prints nothing.With nothing to look for it answers in German.\fBfind\fRdoes the same job without a shell..SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOfind, whereis